        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">St. Peter's Basilica</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1506 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Planned by Popes Nicholas V and Julius II; designed principally by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donato-bramante">Donato Bramante</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlo-maderno">Carlo Maderno</a>, with the square and fittings by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gian-lorenzo-bernini">Gian Lorenzo Bernini</a>; the dome was completed by Giacomo della Porta and Domenico Fontana</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Form</span><span class="info-stat-val">A cruciform church in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> style with a Latin-cross nave and a central dome 136.57 metres high and 41.47 metres across inside; an exterior area of 21,095 square metres and an interior area of 15,160 square metres</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where it is now</span><span class="info-stat-val">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vatican-city">Vatican City</a>, west of the River <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiber-river">Tiber</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janiculum">Janiculum</a> Hill and Hadrian's Mausoleum, at the head of St. Peter's Square</span></div>
